    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90437.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 94,
    "turn_text": "Well, don't worry about me, but worry about the country. This country is great. We all believe in America that it could stand anything. One term even of Donald Trump. Two terms, I think, does very serious damage to the institutions of our democracy. Very serious. So, as I say, we don't agonize. We organize. We're going to make sure we have to win this election. Last time, maybe, overcompetize whatever it was, Russian intervention, whatever it was, change the outcome. But in this election, we must win. Nothing less is at stake than our democracy, our Constitution, The, well, who are we? The United States of America, this beautiful country, our Constitution. He's shredding. He dishonors the Constitution. Who are we? A nation of immigrants by and large, aren't we proud of our presidential ticket? A nation of immigrants. And he denigrates who we are as a people. What are we? A beautiful land from Sita's shining sea and beyond that God gave us. And he degrades it every single day. Well, let's say maybe five times a week. And then, well, who are we? We are a nation of values, of community. vision of our founders of that, he played bassoon him of bringing people together, and he undermines that. And that matters will only get worse if he's allowed to be left to his own devices on this. And what's the saddest part of it all are the Republicans in Congress, just catering. And then people say, oh, in the cloak room, they may say something else. No, they don't, because they share his views politically. They don't care about the environment. They're in the pocket of the fossil fuel industry. They don't care about safety for our children. They're in the pocket of the gun industry. They don't care about fairness in our economy. What are we talking about? He's their guy. He's their guy. He's doing exactly what they want. Now, they're not disgusting personally. I mean, I don't know how they are because I don't know, but I assume they're not, but they're not publicly as disgusting as he is personally, but they're willing to accept that because that's where they are politically. Look, 80-some percent of the Republicans support what Trump is doing. 80-some percent. What a day that it's not 90%. So this elections have ramifications. May I say to my Republican friends, and I do have some, take back your party. America needs a strong Republican party. This is the grand old party. You've done great things for our country. This isn't who you are. You've been hijacked. You've been hijacked by people who don't even want to, you mentioned Meadows, he didn't even vote for Sandy A. No, it's just to show you where those people are. So, take it back because we don't, we want to be the preeminent part. We intend to have a big victory. I know they'll try to steal it. They'll try to lie, cheat and steal, to steal it. But we have to inoculate against that. And we cannot allow them to scare people from voting because It's only going to be a mess. That's a technique, a tactic that they have, and we cannot let them get away with it. But it is sad to see how the Republicans have been so delinquent, derelict in their duty to protect the Constitution and our country and honor the legacy of the Republican Party.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
